{
    "test_name": "MOB.807_Search_MultiValue_Enum_Record",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.807_Search_MultiValue_Enum_Record",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.807` **`MultiValueSelector`'s `enum` and `record` branches** \u2014 checklist \ud83d\udfe2 #1.\n- `MOB.806` covers the `TagsInput` branch; this covers the other two, with fields chosen\n  from the runtime schema read over the API (trap 15): `Failure Curve` (enum) and\n  `Asset Type` (record).\n- \u2b50 **Enum, end to end**: options pre-loaded without typing, `flat` picked, `Add Filter`\n  live, pill `Failure Curve includes flat`, and the list re-queried (its first rows change).\n- \ud83d\udfe1 **Record (bugs \u00a739)**: options arrive from the server and a pick makes the draft valid,\n  but `addFilter` reads `.label` off an ARRAY, so the filter is saved with no value \u2014 the pill\n  shows none, and the server ignores the condition (303 of 303 assets, measured). Two\n  OPTIONAL sentinels record it.\n- Pick steps go through the MultiSelect's own listbox (`aria-controls`), never a bare\n  `role=option`, which could hit a stale Field/Operator option (trap 3).\n- READ-ONLY: both filters are cleared `always`.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Search",
            "StructuredQuery",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
